diff --git a/CHANGES.md b/CHANGES.md
index 14e8f85b..67d273c5 100644
--- a/CHANGES.md
+++ b/CHANGES.md
@@ -10,6 +10,12 @@
 * Standardized parser normalization of tag and attribute names so that HTML comparisons use ASCII-only case folding, and accepted control characters are preserved, aligning name handling to the HTML and XML specs. [#2594](https://github.com/jhy/jsoup/issues/2594)
 * Named character references without a semicolon before `-` or `_` now decode correctly in attribute values, matching HTML and browser behavior (e.g., `&copy-` becomes `©-`). [#2588](https://github.com/jhy/jsoup/issues/2588)
 * Support downloads > 2GB via `Response.bodyStream()` when `maxBodySize(0)` is configured. [#2593](https://github.com/jhy/jsoup/issues/2593)
+* Fixed table foster parenting in the HTML parser, for both documents and fragments:
+  * The adoption agency algorithm now fosters out of the table, rather than moving the block into the table. E.g. `<table><b><p>X</b>` now produces `<b></b><p><b>X</b></p><table></table>`.
+  * Consecutive paragraphs (e.g. `<table><tr><p id=first><p id=second>`) are now both fostered, in input order.
+  * Foster parenting now respects an intervening `template`.
+  * An errant `</col>` no longer closes the current column group, and EOF in a column group follows the normal body and template cleanup.
+  * Fragment parsing now uses a synthetic `html` stack root, rather than a copy of the context element. So the context can't be closed or re-nested by its content. E.g. setting a `tr`'s HTML to `<tr><td>One</td></tr>` now produces just `<td>One</td>`. Setting a `colgroup`'s HTML to `<tr><col>` now produces just `<col>`. Streamed fragment nodes now stay within the result container.

 ## 1.23.2 (2026-Aug-26)

